{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: amendment 4 lanes L/B revision 2 at 2439cb6417b30d05023c0e0f723cefacf6e67a46, all 22 artifacts with notes/amendment4-log.md first. Review 74f29c21's 32-bit logical-length narrowing is fixed without a logical-entry cap.\n\nArchitecture: Float64Array preserves safe-integer logical lengths through segment planning, Body, batching, hashing and sending. Placement and chunking use the original lengths; segments validate that their total is also an exact safe integer. Layout 2 continues to put only the chunk stub in its bounded segment. Lazy eachChunk avoids eagerly allocating a chunk descriptor list before any body is read, while keeping one size/offset rule shared with chunks(). RetainedRef requires both a reader and a nonnegative safe-integer size when either is supplied, preventing the NaN/negative empty-hash result and Infinity loop. The five follow-up files were read as complete diffs; the sixth combined blob is Git's index exporting both the reviewed amendment-4 outcomes and landed founding helpers. All other blobs match fully reviewed V1 or approved main. The 22 changed paths exactly match the artifacts; no main paths are deleted and merge 2439cb64 overwrites no disjoint parent changes. Landed founding and MCP stage 0 are preserved.\n\nSecurity/correctness: a source that changes its length between measurement and hashing or between hashing and sending is still rejected before a push. New tests cover both layouts at the 2^32 boundary, invalid retained sizes and incomplete reader/size pairs, segment-total overflow, and a chunked source changing during send. The previously reviewed digest, signature, immutable-segment reuse, layout-switch boundary and both CAS-order controls remain in the passing suites. The known remote object-bound refusal remains distinct from landed, unknown and lease outcomes.\n\nSimplification: a precise length representation repairs the defect at its shared type rather than introducing special handling for individual large entries. eachChunk owns validation and iteration; chunks() is just its list form. The existing source-change checks remain useful and are not weakened to accommodate wrapping.\n\nIndependent verification: fresh npm ci (374 packages), root typecheck and root npm test all passed: 1,834 tests total (1,641 Vitest and 193 native Node), with one existing Vitest skip. Git's additional Workers suite passed eight tests and its local real-git log suite passed 12, including hook refusal. Seven independent boundary controls against the actual commitFor passed: 2^32-1, 2^32 and 2^32+1 in both layouts, plus Number.MAX_SAFE_INTEGER in layout 2. Each correct logical length reaches the deliberate body-read stop without the former false source-change error. These are metadata/control-flow controls; no 4 GiB or maximum-size body was allocated or fully hashed, and they are not claims of a complete signed publication at those sizes. The candidate's real byte publication/verification tests cover B+1 entries and 20 MiB retained files. git diff --check passed, diagnostics were excluded from baseline discovery and removed, and the worktree is clean. Logs, boundary controls and byte/merge manifests are under /tmp/artroom-checker-log-Am4-LB-v2*. Builder mutation claims were read, not independently repeated.\n\nThis approves the stated L/B implementation. The coordinated live layout-2 checks remain due. Whole logical-file readers still reassemble results, and Room adoption, durable tracking of every unresolved publication outcome/admin attention, large-entry API/subscribe behavior, full verifier transition reconstruction and the broader platform integration remain under their separate requests. The Workers log suite took 211 seconds in this local run; this is gate evidence, not a deployed throughput or memory guarantee. No live deployment or live credential operation was performed.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:10b6f9e98d5d0311d6d